      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Foundation of the Mughal Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Mughal Empire was founded by Babur in 1526 after defeating Ibrahim Lodi in the First Battle of Panipat.",
        "Humayun succeeded Babur but lost his throne temporarily to Sher Shah Suri before regaining it.",
        "Akbar the Great strengthened administrative unity through the Mansabdari system and religious tolerance.",
        "Mughal art and architecture reached its peak during the reign of Shah Jahan.",
        "Aurangzeb expanded the empire to its maximum territorial extent, but his policies accelerated its decline."
      ],
      "id": "r4li9f6"
    },
